[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Whether the board renders plans or work

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-TUI-BOARD-SUBJECT
TITLE: Whether the board renders plans or work
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: open
RETIRES_ON: >>>
The TUI's backend is specified against a real data layer rather than fixtures.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The kanban prototype's data model is the earlier overlay's -- TASK, PLAN,
MILESTONE, a work STATUS spanning open through done, and blocking edges. The
grammar in use has none of those: no work-status field anywhere, no milestone,
and node types that describe design rather than work.

A board over the PLAN would reintroduce the work store the plan deliberately
does not keep. A board over the execution engine, fed by the plan at ingest, is
the shape that survives MECH-PLAN-CHANGE-KINDS.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Recorded now because the divergence is invisible while the backend is fixtures
and expensive once it is not. The prototype labels itself honestly -- fixture
backend, no SDoc writes -- so nothing is wrong yet; this is only the fork that
gets chosen when the fixtures are replaced.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Not a criticism of the prototype, which is deliberately unspecced at this
layer. The operator raised the same gap independently.
<<<
